            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="notes">
        <div class="note">
          <h3>franz-go</h3>
          <p>Its defaults are already its strongest settings. Clean through every fault, and no send failed in 27 runs.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          <h3>sarama · kafka-go</h3>
          <p>On their defaults, a leader crash loses writes the client reported as done. Both libraries document this.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="note">
          <h3>confluent-kafka-go</h3>
          <p>Its defaults wait for every copy but aren't idempotent, so a retry can store a message twice.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="panel-foot">
        <span>Each cell is three runs, five for sarama's defaults in the first crash. Apache Kafka 4.3.1.</span>
        <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/omkar619-dev/driftlab#findings-so-far" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Read the full write-up ↗</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== numbers ===== -->
  <section class="band tight" aria-label="driftlab in numbers">
    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="num">10</div>
        <div class="what">issues reported upstream</div>
        <div class="where">nats.go, franz-go, sarama, kaf-relay, Blnk</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="num ok">4</div>
        <div class="what">fixed</div>
        <div class="where">nats.go v1.55.0; Blnk main, not released yet</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="num review">3</div>
        <div class="what">fixes in review</div>
        <div class="where">nats.go, franz-go, sarama</div>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <div class="num">7</div>
        <div class="what">projects tested</div>
        <div class="where">4 Kafka clients, nats.go, kaf-relay, Blnk</div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="checked">Statuses checked on GitHub on 7 November 2026.</p>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== findings ===== -->
  <section class="band" id="findings" aria-labelledby="findings-title">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="label">Findings</span>
      <h2 id="findings-title">What broke, and where it stands</h2>
      <p class="lede">Every finding links to its report upstream, with the run that shows it.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="findings">
      <article class="card wide">
        <div class="card-head">
          <h3>Blnk</h3>
          <span class="ver">v0.15.7</span>
          <span class="kind">ledger</span>
        </div>
        <div class="issues">
          <div class="issue">
            <p>Transfers answered <code>201 QUEUED</code> were lost if the API server stopped before its background save.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status fixed">Fixed in main</span><a href="https://github.com/blnkfinance/blnk/issues/418" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 418 ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/blnkfinance/blnk/pull/425" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fix 425 ↗</a></div>
          </div>
          <div class="issue">
            <p>The worker built batches around transfers it had already applied, then tried each batch again.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status fixed">Fixed in main</span><a href="https://github.com/blnkfinance/blnk/issues/421" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 421 ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/blnkfinance/blnk/pull/423" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fix 423, tested ↗</a></div>
          </div>
          <div class="issue">
            <p>Under load, balance updates deadlocked with transaction inserts in Postgres.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status fixed">Fixed in main</span><a href="https://github.com/blnkfinance/blnk/issues/422" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 422 ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/blnkfinance/blnk/pull/424" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fix 424 ↗</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <h3>nats.go</h3>
          <span class="ver">v1.53.1, v1.54.0</span>
          <span class="kind">NATS client</span>
        </div>
        <div class="issues">
          <div class="issue">
            <p>The <code>jetstream</code> ordered consumer used a 15-second heartbeat instead of 5, so it took 30 seconds to notice a silent line.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status fixed">Fixed in v1.55.0</span><a href="https://github.com/nats-io/nats.go/issues/2181" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 2181 ↗</a></div>
          </div>
          <div class="issue">
            <p>The push ordered consumer goes silent for up to about 14 seconds after reconnecting, with no error.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status review">Fix in review</span><a href="https://github.com/nats-io/nats.go/issues/2180" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 2180 ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/nats-io/nats.go/pull/2201" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fix 2201, checked ↗</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <h3>sarama</h3>
          <span class="ver">v1.61.1</span>
          <span class="kind">Kafka client</span>
        </div>
        <div class="issues">
          <div class="issue">
            <p>The idempotent producer can wait out its whole 30-second read timeout on a frozen broker, after the partition already takes writes again.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status review">Fix in review</span><a href="https://github.com/IBM/sarama/issues/3843" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 3843 ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/IBM/sarama/pull/3849" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fix 3849 ↗</a></div>
          </div>
          <div class="issue">
            <p>With its default settings, a leader crash loses acknowledged messages. In three of five runs it lost everything written so far, 521 to 526 messages.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status doc">Documented</span><a href="https://github.com/omkar619-dev/driftlab#findings-so-far" target="_blank" rel="noopener">the runs ↗</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <h3>franz-go</h3>
          <span class="ver">v1.20.7, v1.22.2</span>
          <span class="kind">Kafka client</span>
        </div>
        <div class="issues">
          <div class="issue">
            <p>A request whose context has ended keeps waiting while another request to the same broker dials, 10 seconds by default.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status review">Fix in review</span><a href="https://github.com/twmb/franz-go/issues/1505" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 1505 ↗</a><a href="https://github.com/twmb/franz-go/pull/1506" target="_blank" rel="noopener">fix 1506, checked ↗</a></div>
          </div>
          <div class="issue">
            <p>After a leader crash, the reader finds the new leader up to 5 seconds later than it could.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status reported">Reproduced</span><a href="https://github.com/twmb/franz-go/issues/1531" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 1531 ↗</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <article class="card">
        <div class="card-head">
          <h3>kaf-relay</h3>
          <span class="ver">v2.1.0</span>
          <span class="kind">Kafka relay</span>
        </div>
        <div class="issues">
          <div class="issue">
            <p>A restart while the copy can't commit leaves a duplicate in it, and the next restart skips a message, with no error.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status reported">Reported</span><a href="https://github.com/zerodha/kaf-relay/issues/49" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 49 ↗</a></div>
          </div>
          <div class="issue">
            <p>A relay doesn't start while the copy has caught up, and it retries fetch errors with no backoff.</p>
            <div class="meta"><span class="status reported">Reported</span><a href="https://github.com/zerodha/kaf-relay/issues/48" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 48 ↗</a></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== method ===== -->
  <section class="band" id="method" aria-labelledby="method-title">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="label">Method</span>
      <h2 id="method-title">Drive it, record it, check it</h2>
      <p class="lede">The history is the interface between running a test and judging it. The checker never touches the network, so an old run can be judged again after a checker fix, without running anything.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="steps">
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">1 · Drive</span>
        <h3>A real client, a real fault</h3>
        <p>A driver runs one scenario against a real broker or service and injects the fault on cue: a leader crash, a frozen follower, a cut link, a stalled consumer.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">2 · Record</span>
        <h3>One line per operation</h3>
        <p>Each send and its acknowledgement, each delivery, each fault and each error the client reported goes into the history as one JSON line, in the order it happened.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="step">
        <span class="n">3 · Check</span>
        <h3>Every acknowledged write</h3>
        <p>The checker reads the history afterwards. Every acknowledged message must arrive once and in order, and the consumer must catch up on its own.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <div class="history">
        <div class="pane-head"><span>history.jsonl</span><span>excerpt</span></div>
<pre><span class="q">&#123;"type":</span><span class="s">"meta"</span><span class="q">,"client":</span><span class="s">"github.com/nats-io/nats.go@v1.53.1"</span><span class="q">,"api":</span><span class="s">"legacy"</span><span class="q">,"scenario":</span><span class="s">"slow-short"</span><span class="q">, …&#125;</span>
<span class="q">&#123;"index":</span>0<span class="q">,"time_ns":</span>0<span class="q">,"process":</span><span class="s">"producer"</span><span class="q">,"type":</span><span class="s">"invoke"</span><span class="q">,"f":</span><span class="s">"publish"</span><span class="q">,"value":</span>1<span class="q">&#125;</span>
<span class="q">&#123;"index":</span>1<span class="q">,"time_ns":</span>410000<span class="q">,"process":</span><span class="s">"producer"</span><span class="q">,"type":</span><span class="s">"ok"</span><span class="q">,"f":</span><span class="s">"publish"</span><span class="q">,"value":</span>1<span class="q">,"stream_seq":</span>1<span class="q">&#125;</span>
<span class="q">&#123;"index":</span>2<span class="q">,"time_ns":</span>502000000<span class="q">,"process":</span><span class="s">"consumer"</span><span class="q">,"type":</span><span class="s">"ok"</span><span class="q">,"f":</span><span class="s">"deliver"</span><span class="q">,"value":</span>1<span class="q">,"stream_seq":</span>1<span class="q">&#125;</span>
<span class="q">&#123;"index":</span>3<span class="q">,"time_ns":</span>502050000<span class="q">,"process":</span><span class="f">"nemesis"</span><span class="q">,"type":</span><span class="s">"invoke"</span><span class="q">,"f":</span><span class="f">"overflow"</span><span class="q">&#125;</span>
<span class="q">&#123;"index":</span>4<span class="q">,"time_ns":</span>502100000<span class="q">,"process":</span><span class="f">"nemesis"</span><span class="q">,"type":</span><span class="s">"invoke"</span><span class="q">,"f":</span><span class="f">"stall"</span><span class="q">&#125;</span>
<span class="q">&#123;"index":</span>5<span class="q">,"time_ns":</span>611000000<span class="q">,"process":</span><span class="s">"consumer"</span><span class="q">,"type":</span><span class="s">"info"</span><span class="q">,"f":</span><span class="s">"client-error"</span><span class="q">,"error":</span><span class="s">"nats: slow consumer, messages dropped"</span><span class="q">&#125;</span></pre>
      </div>
      <div class="verdict">
        <div class="pane-head"><span>driftlab check</span><span>verdict</span></div>
        <div class="verdict-body">
          <div class="result">Failed: poll-skip</div>
          <dl class="kv">
            <dt>never delivered</dt><dd>values 21 to 100</dd>
            <dt>caught up</dt><dd>never</dd>
            <dt>run</dt><dd>nats.go v1.53.1, legacy API, slow-short, 6 Oct 2026</dd>
          </dl>
          <div class="after">The same scenario on v1.54.0, which has the fix: <strong>clean</strong>, caught up in 18 s.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="calibrated">
      <h3>Calibrated first</h3>
      <p>A checker has to catch a known bug before its clean results mean anything. The run above is that test for the NATS checks: nats.go <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/nats-io/nats.go/issues/2107" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 2107</a>, caught on v1.53.1 and clean on v1.54.0. The Kafka checks passed the same test on franz-go <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/twmb/franz-go/issues/1217" target="_blank" rel="noopener">issue 1217</a> and sarama <a class="inline-link" href="https://github.com/IBM/sarama/pull/3762" target="_blank" rel="noopener">pull request 3762</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ===== ledgers ===== -->
  <section class="band" id="ledgers" aria-labelledby="ledgers-title">
    <div class="head">
      <span class="label">Ledgers</span>
      <h2 id="ledgers-title">A ledger that answered before it saved, fixed in 4 days</h2>
      <p class="lede">Blnk is an open-source double-entry ledger. In v0.15.7 its API replied <code>201 QUEUED</code> as soon as a transfer was handed to a background save, so a server that stopped in between lost transfers it had already answered for. driftlab reported that and two smaller bugs on 2 November. Blnk fixed all three by 5 November, and on 6 November the same runs against its main branch lost nothing.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="ledger-grid">
      <div class="box">
        <p class="box-title">One stop, five seconds in</p>
        <div class="bignum">6,011</div>
        <p class="bignum-cap">transfers answered <code>201 QUEUED</code> and never saved, after <code>docker stop</code> five seconds into a full-speed run on v0.15.7.</p>
        <div class="after-fix"><span class="to">0</span><span>on Blnk's main, which saves each transfer before it answers. Same stop, same kill, same frozen Postgres.</span></div>
        <p class="bignum-note">Balances matched in every run, and no transfer was applied twice. The damage was to completeness: the caller held a 201 and a transaction ID that the ledger had no record of.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="box">
        <p class="box-title">How far the saves fell behind the answers, no fault</p>
        <svg class="chart" viewBox="0 0 560 238" role="img" aria-label="Transfers answered but not yet saved, by send rate, on v0.15.7: kept up at 100 a second, 1,498 behind at 200, 2,957 at 400, 12,601 at 800. On Blnk's main at 800 a second: none.">
          <text class="muted" x="0" y="14">v0.15.7</text>
          <text class="muted" x="96" y="14">answered but not yet saved, at the worst moment</text>
          <!-- scale: 12,601 = 380px, bars start at x = 96 -->
          <text class="axis-label" x="0" y="52">100 / s</text>
          <rect class="track" x="96" y="38" width="380" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <text class="val keptup" x="104" y="53">kept up</text>
          <text class="axis-label" x="0" y="94">200 / s</text>
          <rect class="track" x="96" y="80" width="380" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <rect class="bar-soft" x="96" y="80" width="45.2" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <text class="val" x="149" y="95">1,498</text>
          <text class="axis-label" x="0" y="136">400 / s</text>
          <rect class="track" x="96" y="122" width="380" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <rect class="bar-soft" x="96" y="122" width="89.2" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <text class="val" x="193" y="137">2,957</text>
          <text class="axis-label" x="0" y="178">800 / s</text>
          <rect class="track" x="96" y="164" width="380" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <rect class="bar" x="96" y="164" width="380" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <text class="val" x="484" y="179">12,601</text>
          <line class="divider" x1="0" y1="198" x2="560" y2="198"/>
          <text class="axis-label" x="0" y="226">main 800</text>
          <rect class="track" x="96" y="212" width="380" height="20" rx="3"/>
          <text class="val keptup" x="104" y="227">0, it saves before it answers</text>
        </svg>
        <p class="chart-note">On v0.15.7 every one of those answers still came back in 1 to 2 ms, and a crash at that moment lost the whole gap. On main an answer waits for its save: 10 ms at the median, 31 ms at the 99th percentile.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

